# Talaria PHP SDK

Language-agnostic ingest adapter for Talaria. Primary target: PHP / Silverstripe apps.

## Role

```
App → TalariaClient
        ├─ capture* / Logger     → EventQueue → POST /events/ingestBatch
        └─ Tracer (optional APM) → SpanQueue  → POST /spans/ingestBatch
```

- Fingerprinting and issue grouping are **server-side only** — never compute fingerprints here
- Auth: project API key via `X-API-Key` (`tal_live_…`). Default app keys include `eventsWrite` + `spansWrite`
- Always send via **batch** ingest; never one HTTP call per log or span in the normal path
- Never wrap `ServerpodHttpTransport` or `SpanTransport` Guzzle clients with tracing middleware
- No billing APIs; treat 429 carefully (quota vs rate limit)

## Package map

| Path | Role |
| ---- | ---- |
| `src/` | Framework-agnostic SDK (`Talaria\`) |
| `silverstripe/src/` | Thin Silverstripe adapter (`Talaria\SilverStripe\`) |
| `silverstripe/handlers/` | Monolog 1/2/3 handlers — factory `require_once` only, not PSR-4 |
| `client/` | Docs for npm `@newtalaria/browser` (loaded via jsDelivr, not vendored) |
| `_config/` | Silverstripe YAML (vendormodule discovery) |
| `tests/` | PHPUnit |

## Vocabulary

| Term | SDK responsibility |
| ---- | ------------------ |
| Event | Build wire JSON (message, level, stack, tags, extra, environment, release) |
| level | Severity: `debug` \| `info` \| `warning` \| `error` \| `fatal` |
| eventType | Derived from level when omitted (`fatal`/`error` → `error`) |
| environment | `production` \| `staging` \| `development` |
| sampleRate | Client-side event sampling before enqueue |
| enableTracing / tracesSampleRate | APM off until enabled; head-based span sampling (100% errors, default 10% success) |

## Sources of truth

- Live ingest: Talaria server `events/ingestBatch` and `spans/ingestBatch` (Serverpod RPC)
- Parity reference: `@newtalaria/browser` transport (same camelCase + `__className__`)
- Prefer live server behavior over `new_talaria/planning/php_sdk` prototype when they diverge

## Silverstripe logging stack

- Target CMS: **4.13+ / 5 / 6** (PHP 8.1+)
- Allow `monolog ^1.25 \|\| ^3` and `psr/log ^1 \|\| ^2 \|\| ^3` — stock SS4 uses Monolog 1 + `psr/log` 1; SS5/6 use Monolog 3 + `psr/log` 2\|3
- Dual handlers under `silverstripe/handlers/` (not PSR-4); factory `require_once`s one file; never a generic `TalariaLogHandler` class

## Explicit don'ts

- Do not compute fingerprints
- Do not call `events/ingest` for normal or flush paths — always `ingestBatch`
- Do not retry unbounded on 429
- Do not import Silverstripe types from `src/`
- Do not pin `psr/log` to `^3` only (breaks SS4 and some SS5 resolves)
- Do not Composer-autoload Monolog-specific handler classes (loading Monolog 3 handler on Monolog 1 fatals before the factory runs)
- Do not type `Talaria\Logger::log()` `$message` / `$level` (breaks psr/log 1.x `LoggerInterface`)
